 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:BEGIN TeslaAutoTurnSignals -->
 <!-- CARROT:REVIEW reviewed-for="" -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+Requests left/right lamps from existing ATC turn/lane-change decisions, holds through finishing, then cancels its own request. Automatic feedback is not driver confirmation. Physical stalk input and hazards take priority. Invalid feedback cancels the request; unconfirmed cancellation stops further automatic output for this onroad cycle.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+Default OFF; reboot after changing. Requires supported Model 3/Y, the vehicle CAN bus, fresh physical stalk input and matching Panda firmware. It does not grant steering or departure permission. Validate both directions and failure/manual takeover on the exact vehicle in a closed course before road use. CAN or device power loss cannot guarantee lamp cancellation.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+Execution: `openpilot/selfdrive/car/tesla_turn_signals.py`. Intent: `openpilot/selfdrive/controls/lib/desire_helper.py`. Safety: `opendbc_repo/opendbc/safety/safety/safety_tesla_turn_signals.h`. See the Tesla user guide for diagnostics and limitations.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:END TeslaAutoTurnSignals -->
